# Bandit Level 18 → Level 19

## Goal

Read the `readme` file in bandit18’s home directory to retrieve the bandit19 password.

The challenge is that `.bashrc` has been modified to log me out when I open a normal SSH session.

## Commands used

From my Ubuntu terminal:

ssh -p 2220 bandit18@bandit.labs.overthewire.org "ls"
ssh -p 2220 bandit18@bandit.labs.overthewire.org "cat readme"
ssh -p 2220 bandit19@bandit.labs.overthewire.org

After logging in as bandit19:

whoami

## Explanation

### 1. Identify the login problem

A normal SSH login displayed `Byebye!` and disconnected me.

The level instructions explained that `.bashrc`, a Bash startup file, had been modified to cause this.

My approach was to run a command directly through SSH instead of opening an interactive session.

### 2. List the remote files

ssh -p 2220 bandit18@bandit.labs.overthewire.org "ls"

- `-p 2220` specifies Bandit’s SSH port.
- `bandit18` is the account used to connect.
- `"ls"` tells SSH to execute that command on the remote server.

I entered the bandit18 password. The command listed the files, including `readme`, then the connection closed because the command had finished.

### 3. Read the password file

ssh -p 2220 bandit18@bandit.labs.overthewire.org "cat readme"

This used the same method to display the contents of `readme`.

The output contained the bandit19 password.

### 4. Log in as bandit19

ssh -p 2220 bandit19@bandit.labs.overthewire.org

I entered the retrieved password and checked my account:

whoami

Expected output:

bandit19

## Result

I retrieved the password by running `cat readme` directly through SSH and used it to access bandit19.

## What I learned

- SSH can execute individual commands on a remote machine.
- An interactive session is not always needed to complete a task.
- Shell startup files can affect login behaviour.
- When a remote command finishes, SSH normally closes the connection.

## Problems and fixes

- **Normal login immediately disconnected me:** I supplied a command at the end of the SSH command.
- **The connection closed after showing the file:** This was expected because the remote command had finished.
